DESCRIPTION:Movie: The Time of Cats\nRuntime: 26 min\nDirector: Polina Doro
 feeva\nGenre: Documentary\n\nValentina knows all too well what it means to 
 be responsible for those we have tamed. She runs the Time of Cats shelter w
 hile also working as a lawyer and raising two children. The shelter began a
 s a cat café in the city center\, where 250 cats found new homes over five 
 years. But after a disagreement with the landlord\, it had to move to the o
 utskirts and become a shelter\, making it less convenient for visitors. Tod
 ay\, Time of Cats is home to more than 90 cats\, and despite the help of vo
 lunteers\, the responsibility for them rests largely on Valentina. Finding 
 funding and dealing with the cats’ daily needs take up much of her life. No
 w another problem has emerged: the owner plans to sell the building. Once a
 gain\, the shelter must find a new home.
